ies a holding cost of $4.02 per unit, a shortage penalty of $23.143 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. Finished drone inventory is also checked every 1 day, with holding cost at $7.929 per unit and shortage cost at $0.814 per unit. Demand comes from Ross Associates, which places orders for drone at intervals between 27 days and 32 days, with order volumes ranging from 2618505.0 units to 4829326.0 units. Customer lead time runs between 6 days and 20 days. If stock is not available, the sale is lost rather than backordered. Each drone sells at $2218.162 per unit, and customer payments arrive 30 days later. The model runs for 365 days, with the first 50 days treated as warm-up, and it is set up with 1 replication.

