re, and this cycle is a consistent 3.0 days. The operation also has access to an Injection Molder with capacity for 3 units, a service time ranging from 5.247 days to 8.353 days, and an operating cost of $11.639 per day. On the finished goods side, smartphone stock starts at 3710141 units, carries a shortage cost of $1.461 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day, while tablet inventory starts at 1875916 units. Customer demand comes from Schneider Electric for smartphones and ABB Industrial for tablets. Schneider Electric places orders with an exponential interarrival pattern averaging 29.0 days, with demand typically 3333878.0 units and variability of about 888226.0 units, and expects delivery in 5.0 days to 17.0 days. Any smartphone shortfall is backordered, the selling price is $1414.351 per unit, and payment is received 30.0 days later. ABB Industrial orders tablets with arrivals averaging 44.0 days, volumes anywhere from 1569.0 units to 142426.0 units, and delivery lead times between 16.0 days and 28.0 days. If tablets are unavailable, the sale is lost, and they are sold at $4713.541 per unit with customer payment collected between 22.0 days and 69.0 days. The model runs over a 200-day horizon, with results measured after a warm-up period of 50 days, and 10 replications are used.

