ith interarrival times averaging 18.0 days. Demand is roughly 2033924.0 units on average, varying by about 607734.0 units, and customer deliveries are promised in anywhere from 7.0 days to 25.0 days. Tablet sells at $1197.908 per unit, customers pay between 47.0 days and 72.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. NXP Semiconductors purchases FPGA, with orders arriving on average every 34.0 days. Its order volume ranges from 1045556.0 units to 4644174.0 units, delivery lead time runs between 17.0 days and 24.0 days, and the selling price is $682.875 per unit. Payment comes exactly 52.0 days after delivery, and the fulfillment approach is partial shipment with the remainder backordered. Overall, the modeled network links 2 suppliers—PolymerSource and GlassCore Ltd.—to 3 facilities—Production Center, Main Factory, and Storage Facility—and runs for a 500-day horizon, with results collected after a 30-day warm-up period and 1 replication.

