ts is the second solder_paste source, faster but still variable, with an exponential lead time averaging 2.0 days, a cost of $232.642 per unit, payment due 39.0 days after receipt, and capacity capped at 361512 units; its transfer to Pilot Line runs between 7.0 and 9.0 days. Plastic_pellet comes from Process Go. with a fixed 9.0-day lead time at $221.647 per unit and payment due between 12.0 and 44.0 days, and from FastChip Corp. with a 5.0 to 6.0 day lead time, a much lower price of $27.948 per unit, payment terms between 24.0 and 65.0 days, and a maximum order size of 270966 units. Memory_chip is supplied by CarbonSupply Co. in exactly 7.0 days at $473.524 per unit, with net 34.0 days payment and capacity up to 996550 units; transport from CarbonSupply Co. to Pilot Line takes between 4.0 and 13.0 days. A second source, Memory Star, delivers memory_chip in 3.0 to 17.0 days at $453.33 per unit, with payment due in 20.0 to 51.0 days and capacity of 94312 units, feeding Pilot Line directly. The operating footprint includes Pilot Line, Main Factory, Fab, and the Regional Depot, with all 6 suppliers linked into those 4 facilities through the network. Pilot Line manages heat_sink, plastic_pellet, and medical_device, and runs a cutting step that converts heat_sink and plastic_pellet into medical_device in 15.0 to 28.0 days using the CNC Machine. That CNC Machine has capacity for 4 units at a time, works with an exponential processing time averaging 4.739 days, and batches jobs in lots of 15 units with a maximum wait of 3.186 days. It also experiences failures: uptime averages 268.639 days before a stop, downtime averages 34.285 days, and operating cost is $17.695 per day. Main Factory handles heat_sink, solder_paste, and solar_panel, where an inspection step turns solder_paste and heat_sink into solar_panel in a steady 11.0 days. Fab manages heat_sink, solder_paste, memory_chip, and router, and its inspection process converts memory_chip, solder_paste, and heat_sink into 