 per unit, and settles invoices 20.0 days later; if stock is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Ross Associates is another router customer, with orders coming every 33.0 to 44.0 hours and demand ranging from 2123513.0 units to 4273274.0 units. Its delivery lead time is fixed at 16.0 hours, the selling price is $1505.55 per unit, and payment comes 44.0 days after receipt; any unmet quantity is backordered rather than lost. The modeled network is straightforward: ElectroParts ships gold_wire to Advanced Fab, BatteryTech sends plastic_pellet to Advanced Fab, and Advanced Fab sends router to the Distribution Center. The scenario runs in hours over a 730-hour horizon, with 1 replication.

