hip and the rest is lost. Samsung Electronics orders GPUs anywhere from every 27.0 days to 58.0 days, with demand ranging from 1618165.0 units to 4269294.0 units; customer lead time is 13.0 days, the price is $25.536 per unit, payment comes in 36.0 days to 38.0 days, and it also follows a partial shipment policy with lost remainder. Dell Technologies is the CPU customer, placing orders every 8.0 days for exactly 3613876.0 units, expecting delivery in 28.0 days, paying $3020.025 per unit with payment 17.0 days later; if stock is short, available units go out immediately and the balance is backordered. The model runs over a 730-day horizon, with results collected after a 50-day warm-up period, across 10 replications.

