ssembly into FPGA units. The operation is supported by an Assembly Line resource with capacity for 3 units, a service time ranging from 0.322 hours to 0.741 hours, and an operating cost of $7.396 per hour. Once built, FPGA units move from Main Factory to Distribution Center. Customer demand comes from Apple Supply, with orders arriving every 27.0 to 48.0 hours and order sizes ranging from 2998505.0 units to 4799932.0 units. Delivery to the customer takes exactly 6.0 hours. The sales approach is partial fulfillment with lost remainder, so available FPGA units are shipped and any unmet balance is lost rather than backordered. Apple Supply buys the product at $2576.366 per unit and pays 9.0 hours after delivery. The network therefore links 3 suppliers—Memory Star, CarbonSupply Co., and ChipCo—to 2 facilities, Main Factory and Distribution Center, and the model is run over a 200-hour horizon with 10 replications.

