321 per unit, shortage cost at $21.807 per unit, and reviews every 1 hour. Solar_panel begins with 2427819 units, carries $5.499 per unit in holding cost, and is also reviewed every 1 hour. Customer demand comes from 2 accounts. Sony Electronics buys smartphone, placing orders every 46.0 hours for 2253871.0 units, with a customer lead time of 13.0 hours; if inventory is short, demand is backordered rather than lost. The selling price is $1818.197 per unit, and Sony Electronics pays 17.0 days after delivery. Ross Associates purchases solar_panel with orders arriving exponentially with a mean of 44.0 hours, and each order falls between 341663.0 units and 423858.0 units. Shipments to Ross Associates take 2.0 hours, shortages are backordered, the selling price is $3967.948 per unit, and cash is collected 21.0 days later. The modeled network includes 3 suppliers, 1 Manufacturing Site, and 1 Distribution Center, and it is run over a 200-hour horizon with 1 replication.

