nits are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered. Sony pays between 26.0 days and 32.0 days after receipt, and the selling price is $1585.018 per unit. Ross Associates also buys tablet units, with orders arriving on average every 33.0 hours and demand centered on 4339345.0 units with variability of 361970.0 units. Its customer lead time ranges from 17.0 hours to 25.0 hours, and under shortages the business ships what it has and loses the rest of the sale. Ross Associates pays exactly 48.0 days after delivery, and the tablet sells to this customer at $4381.256 per unit. Material flow is straightforward: gold_wire moves from MetalFab Inc. to Fab, steel_rod goes from Memory Star to Fab, and completed tablet units are sent from Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs for a 200-hour horizon, with results collected after a 30-hour warm-up period, across 10 replications.

