oduct sells at $3309.728 per unit, customer payment comes between 8.0 and 62.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is simply lost. Drone begins with 4493429 units on hand, is also reviewed every 1 hour, has a holding cost of $5.666 per unit, and a shortage cost of $19.134 per unit. Dell Technologies places drone orders with an average arrival interval of 26.0 hours, each for 1550496.0 units, and receives shipments in between 16.0 and 26.0 hours. The drone sells at $1665.825 per unit, payment is collected 36.0 days after delivery, and shortages are handled as lost sales here as well. The network is straightforward: BatteryTech and MetalFab Inc. feed the Assembly Hub with raw materials, and the Assembly Hub sends both industrial_sensor and drone to the Warehouse. The model runs for 500 hours, with the first 50 hours treated as warm-up, and uses 1 replication.

