This network is built around making the industrial_sensor, with sourcing from FastChip Corp., CarbonSupply Co., PolymerSource, PrecisionParts, and GlassCore Ltd., production at the Production Center, and downstream stocking through the Regional Depot. The finished unit is fairly component-heavy: each industrial_sensor uses 3 units of ceramic_substrate, 3 units of gold_wire, 1 unit of copper_wire, 1 unit of cooling_unit, and 2 units of steel_rod. The cooling_unit itself is a made-up sub-assembly that consumes 5 units of copper_wire, 4 units of steel_rod, 2 units of ceramic_substrate, and 4 units of gold_wire. At the plant level, the Production Center manages gold_wire, cooling_unit, ceramic_substrate, steel_rod, industrial_sensor, and copper_wire inventory in one manufacturing location, while the Regional Depot serves as the warehouse in the network. Ceramic_substrate is replenished on a scheduled basis, with order quantities varying uniformly between 41703.0 units and 92194.0 units, and those replenishment lots arrive every 17.0 to 19.0 days. FastChip Corp. supplies that material with a fixed 7.0-day lead time, a purchase cost of $132.869 per unit, payment due 25.0 to 44.0 days after receipt, and transport from FastChip Corp. to the Production Center taking between 4.0 and 10.0 days. Its inventory carrying cost is $8.764 per unit, shortage cost is $18.894 per unit, and stock is reviewed every 10 days. Gold_wire is sourced on demand rather than on a fixed cycle. CarbonSupply Co. provides it in exactly 6.0 days at $11.521 per unit, with net 20.0-day payment terms and a maximum order size of 812678 units. Gold_wire holding cost runs at $6.625 per unit, with inventory reviewed every 20 days. Copper_wire is also demand-driven, and there are 2 supply options. PolymerSource delivers in 15.0 to 27.0 days at $290.181 per unit, with payment due 26.0 to 81.0 days after delivery, and the move into the Production Center takes 8.0 days. GlassCore Ltd. offers the same material with a consistent 9.0-day supplier lead time, a unit cost of $273.014, 48.0-day payment terms, a capacity limit of 232884 units, and a 3.0-day transfer to the plant. Copper_wire inventory carries a holding cost of $7.378 per unit, a shortage penalty of $36.318 per unit, and a 6-day review cadence. Steel_rod follows a periodic replenishment pattern too, with orders fixed at 58621.0 units and arrivals every 3.0 to 21.0 days. PrecisionParts supplies it with a lead time ranging from 14.0 to 15.0 days, a price of $218.671 per unit, payment due in 48.0 to 53.0 days, and a delivery cap of 322783 units. Holding steel_rod costs $3.809 per unit, shortages cost $9.737 per unit, and planners review that stock every 2 days. On the shop floor, molding is the main production step at the Production Center, converting ceramic_substrate, gold_wire, copper_wire, cooling_unit, and steel_rod into industrial_sensor. That operation runs on a fixed 11.0-day cycle and requires the CNC Machine. The CNC Machine has capacity for 4 units, processes work in 5.279 to 7.024 days, batches are enabled at 44 units, and jobs can wait up to 18.437 days to form a batch; its operating cost is $7.268 per day. A Conveyor Belt with capacity 4 supports flow with a constant 4.345-day service time and an operating cost of $11.152 per day. For inventory positions inside the network, cooling_unit starts with 20477 units on hand, has a shortage cost of $0.828 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. The industrial_sensor begins with 4154003 units in stock, incurs $3.976 per unit in holding cost, $12.359 per unit in shortage cost, and is also reviewed every 1 day. Demand comes from Broadcom Limited, which places orders for industrial_sensor with arrivals averaging 23.0 days apart. Order size ranges uniformly from 2130433.0 units to 3407337.0 units, and customer delivery lead time is between 4.0 and 5.0 days. If inventory is short, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered. The sales side is lucrative at $1910.109 per unit, with customer payment received 24.0 days later. Finished industrial_sensor units move from the Production Center to the Regional Depot, and the whole setup is evaluated over a 730-day planning horizon with 10 replications.

