This network is set up to make camera units, with Main Factory handling display_panel, epoxy_compound, memory_chip, carbon_fiber, camera, and lens_assembly inventory, and a Warehouse receiving finished camera output from the plant. The product structure is layered: each display_panel is built from 5 units of epoxy_compound, 2 units of memory_chip, and 1 unit of carbon_fiber, while each lens_assembly uses 1 unit of carbon_fiber. A finished camera then consumes 2 units of epoxy_compound, 4 units of lens_assembly, 4 units of memory_chip, 2 units of display_panel, and 1 unit of carbon_fiber. On the inbound side, memory_chip is supplied on a very long fixed replenishment rhythm of 993.0 days, with deliveries arriving on a uniform 11.0 to 20.0 day range; it carries a holding cost of $8.505 per unit, a shortage cost of $38.868 per unit, and is reviewed every 8 days. Epoxy_compound follows a min-max approach, triggering replenishment when stock falls below 4275.79 units and restoring inventory to 7430.74 units, with holding at $0.336 per unit, shortage at $40.225 per unit, and review every 17 days. Carbon_fiber is sourced on demand. The factory starts with 1864889 units of display_panel on hand, with a holding cost of $3.842 per unit and a 1 day review cycle, plus 2913205 units of lens_assembly already available. Finished camera inventory begins at 2155740 units, with holding cost of $8.002 per unit, shortage cost of $38.009 per unit, and review every 1 day. Supplier coverage is broad. CarbonSupply Co. sends memory_chip with a consistent 6.0 day lead time at $100.882 per unit, and invoices are settled in 22.0 to 43.0 days. PolymerSource also provides memory_chip, but with exactly 24.0 days lead time, a cost of $308.078 per unit, payment in 30.0 to 73.0 days, and a maximum order size of 34238 units. GlobalComponents is another memory_chip source, delivering in anywhere from 1.0 to 16.0 days at $155.518 per unit with 25.0 to 33.0 day payment terms. For epoxy_compound, MegaSupply ships with an exponential lead time averaging 26.0 days, charges $405.69 per unit, and is paid in 24.0 to 32.0 days; its lane into Main Factory adds a 3.0 day transfer. ElectroParts supplies the same material in exactly 14.0 days at $417.97 per unit, allows a fixed 75.0 day payment term, and can deliver up to 775933 units. Carbon_fiber comes from GlassCore Ltd. in 13.0 days at $349.69 per unit with payment due in 40.0 to 64.0 days and a ceiling of 190965 units per order, from ChipCo with an exponential lead time averaging 4.0 days at $59.032 per unit and 51.0 to 88.0 day payment terms plus capacity of 934556 units, and from BatteryTech with an exponential lead time averaging 18.0 days at $80.002 per unit, payment in 44.0 to 68.0 days, and an added transfer time of 6.0 days. Production itself is centered at Main Factory, where the molding step turns epoxy_compound, lens_assembly, memory_chip, display_panel, and carbon_fiber into camera units on a fixed 25.0 day cycle using the Welding Station. That Welding Station has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with service times between 5.932 days and 8.574 days, runs for 445.704 days before failure on average, then stays down for an exponential 26.234 days, and costs $13.006 per day to operate. There is also an Assembly Line with capacity of 2 units, processing work in 4.702 to 6.274 days, and it runs in batches of 53 units with a maximum wait of 18.633 days; its operating cost is $6.192 per day. On the demand side, ABB Industrial orders camera units with arrivals averaging every 9.0 days, request sizes ranging from 730986.0 units to 4809089.0 units, expects delivery in 5.0 to 15.0 days, pays $4566.842 per unit, and settles invoices in 27.0 to 31.0 days; if product is unavailable, the sale is lost. Samsung Electronics places orders every 33.0 to 50.0 days for exactly 3457148.0 units, expects shipment in 1.0 day, buys at $714.84 per unit, and pays in 75.0 days; available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost. Infineon Technologies follows a similar partial-fulfillment approach, ordering every 31.0 to 44.0 days for exactly 4893000.0 units, with customer lead time between 1.0 and 9.0 days, a selling price of $2661.365 per unit, and payment due in 38.0 days. The model runs for a 100 day horizon.

