y into industrial_sensor in exactly 16.0 weeks. Material handling is supported by a Conveyor Belt with capacity for 2 units at a time, service time between 5.199 weeks and 5.54 weeks, batching enabled at 52 units with a maximum wait of 3.18 weeks, uptime fixed at 488.998 weeks, downtime fixed at 47.593 weeks, and an operating cost of $11.96 per week. In terms of network flow, GlobalComponents, PrecisionParts, and MegaSupply all ship directly to Advanced Fab; Advanced Fab then sends both router and industrial_sensor to the Storage Facility. On the demand side, TechCorp buys router every 9.0 weeks, with demand centered around 2470421.0 units and varying by about 388655.0 units. Customer delivery for TechCorp takes between 9.0 weeks and 17.0 weeks, the selling price is $4836.614 per unit, payment comes in between 42.0 days and 43.0 days, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Broadcom Limited orders industrial_sensor anywhere from every 20.0 weeks to 29.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 1531966.0 units to 4685035.0 units. Its delivery time is a consistent 1.0 week, the price is $1516.085 per unit, payment arrives between 27.0 days and 45.0 days, and any unmet demand is backordered until inventory becomes available. The model runs for a 730-week horizon, with results collected after a 30-week warm-up period and evaluated across 5 replications.

