 3869309 units of EV_battery, with a holding cost of $9.032 per unit, a shortage cost of $22.116 per unit, and review every 1 hour. Laptop begins with 1034276 units on hand, has a holding charge of $6.909 per unit, and is also reviewed every 1 hour. Customer demand comes from Apple Supply for EV_battery and Sony Electronics for laptop. Apple Supply places orders at intervals between 12.0 and 59.0 hours, requesting between 169066.0 and 2182801.0 units each time, expects delivery in 13.0 to 23.0 hours, pays $3630.504 per unit, and settles invoices between 16.0 and 82.0 days later; if stock is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Sony Electronics orders laptop every 29.0 to 39.0 hours, with order sizes from 2585692.0 to 3046491.0 units, accepts delivery in 15.0 to 20.0 hours, buys at $1037.266 per unit, and pays exactly 45.0 days after receipt; here too, partial shipments go out and any unmet balance is lost. The model runs for 200 hours overall, with the first 50 hours treated as warm-up, and 10 replications are included.

