This network centers on Advanced Fab, which makes laptops and also keeps the key inputs on hand, with Regional Depot serving as the downstream warehouse. The material base includes glass_fiber, solder_paste, and ceramic_substrate, and there is also a fabricated sub-component called cooling_unit. Each cooling_unit uses 3 units of glass_fiber, 2 units of ceramic_substrate, and 1 unit of solder_paste. Each laptop then requires 4 units of ceramic_substrate, 4 units of cooling_unit, 1 unit of glass_fiber, and 4 units of solder_paste. At the plant, glass_fiber is managed with a min-max style replenishment rule: when stock falls below 4419.28 units, it is brought back up to 6594.0 units. Shortages of glass_fiber carry a penalty of $48.695 per unit, and that stock position is reviewed every 13 weeks. Solder_paste is supplied on a scheduled basis, with deliveries averaging 97995.0 units and varying by about 19040.0 units, arriving every 15.0 weeks. Ceramic_substrate is also controlled with a reorder threshold, triggering replenishment below 279.5 units and restoring inventory to 635.26 units; it has a holding cost of $4.778 per unit, a shortage cost of $30.229 per unit, and a 15-week review cycle. For in-process stock, cooling_unit starts with 933288 units on hand, carries $1.652 per unit in holding cost, and is checked every 1 week. Finished laptops begin with 4821359 units in inventory, and shortages cost $19.273 per unit, with review every 1 week. Supply is split across multiple vendors. GlassCore Ltd. provides glass_fiber with a consistent 20.0-week supplier lead time at $413.03 per unit, and payment is due 75.0 days after delivery; shipments from GlassCore Ltd. to Advanced Fab take 5.0 weeks. FastChip Corp. is the second glass_fiber source, with an exponential lead time averaging 14.0 weeks, a price of $441.027 per unit, and payment terms ranging from 37.0 to 55.0 days; transfer to Advanced Fab takes 7.0 weeks. For solder_paste, PrecisionParts ships with a fixed 12.0-week lead time at $436.684 per unit, with invoices settled in 39.0 to 48.0 days, while GlobalComponents offers the same material in exactly 1.0 week at $10.043 per unit, on 13.0-day payment terms, and can supply up to 283710 units per delivery. Ceramic_substrate comes either from SiliconWorks, whose lead time is exponential with a mean of 1.0 week, charging $15.206 per unit with payment due in 49.0 to 59.0 days and a maximum order size of 126767 units, or from PolymerSource, which delivers in exactly 28.0 weeks at $231.203 per unit, allows 40.0 to 52.0 days to pay, can supply up to 354289 units per order, and takes 5.0 weeks to transfer material to Advanced Fab. Production at Advanced Fab is built around an inspection step that consumes ceramic_substrate, cooling_unit, glass_fiber, and solder_paste and turns them into laptops. That step runs on the Welding Station, with a fixed cycle of 27.0 weeks per job. The Welding Station has capacity for 3 units at a time, works with service times ranging from 0.264 to 7.171 weeks, and uses batching, grouping work into lots of 50 units with a maximum wait of 9.711 weeks before processing. It is not perfectly reliable either: uptime lasts 71.511 weeks flat, followed by 18.773 weeks of downtime, and it costs $13.24 per week to operate. A Packaging Machine is also part of the setup, with capacity for 5 units, a steady 5.556-week processing time, and an operating cost of $13.162 per week. On the demand side, Bosch Automotive buys laptops, placing orders at intervals between 17.0 and 39.0 weeks, with each order fixed at 642826.0 units. Customer lead time runs between 17.0 and 19.0 weeks. If stock is short, available units are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered. The selling price is $3565.172 per unit, and customer payment comes 66.0 days after delivery. In terms of network structure, the suppliers GlassCore Ltd., PrecisionParts, SiliconWorks, FastChip Corp., GlobalComponents, and PolymerSource feed the facilities Advanced Fab and Regional Depot, and laptops move from Advanced Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs in weeks over a 100-week horizon, with results collected after a 30-week warm-up period and evaluated across 10 replications.

