_paste, and glass_fiber into tablet units in anywhere from 8.0 days to 25.0 days. Starting stock is quite large for the semi-finished parts and finished goods: 4018644 units of motor_assembly, 3215489 units of camera, and 302312 units of tablet. The motor_assembly inventory is reviewed every 1 day as well, with a holding charge of $0.434 per unit. On the demand side, ABB Industrial buys camera units, placing orders with exponentially distributed interarrival times averaging 48.0 days. Its demand is centered around 4427636.0 units with variability of about 107822.0 units, delivery to the customer takes between 3.0 days and 23.0 days, the business sells at $2035.404 per unit, and payment is received 10.0 days later. If camera stock is short, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered. Sony Electronics purchases tablet units with order arrivals averaging 59.0 days, demand roughly 714112.0 units with variation of 94145.0 units, and a consistent 27.0-day customer lead time. Tablets are sold at $982.568 per unit, with customer payment coming 33.0 days after delivery, and shortages are handled the same way: what is available ships now and the balance is backordered. Overall, the modeled system runs for 365 days, and the scenario is evaluated across 10 replications.

