ld_wire to Advanced Fab with a lead time between 10.0 weeks and 19.0 weeks, charging $343.811 per unit, offering 27.0-day payment terms, and supporting up to 58338 units per order. ChipCo is the second gold_wire source, a bit tighter on transit at 13.0 weeks to 14.0 weeks, but more expensive at $483.393 per unit, with payment due 60.0 days after delivery. NanoMaterials Inc. supplies resin with lead times between 4.0 weeks and 10.0 weeks at $282.671 per unit and payment terms ranging from 29.0 days to 83.0 days. GlobalComponents handles steel_rod, typically arriving with an average lead time of 27.0 weeks, priced at $104.26 per unit, paid 17.0 days after receipt, and capped at 340220 units per delivery; the movement from GlobalComponents to Advanced Fab itself takes exactly 8.0 weeks. FastChip Corp. supplies solder_paste with an exponential lead time averaging 25.0 weeks, a unit cost of $299.972, and net 72.0-day payment. On the shop floor, the cutting step at Advanced Fab converts steel_rod, resin, and gold_wire into smartphone output in exactly 1.0 week per cycle and uses the Injection Molder. That machine has capacity for 1 unit of work at a time, processes jobs in anywhere from 2.464 weeks to 6.956 weeks, and runs in batches of 97 units with a maximum wait of 8.976 weeks before release. It also fails from time to time: uptime is a consistent 80.631 weeks, downtime averages 21.705 weeks, and operating expense is $11.347 per week. EV_battery fabrication also happens at Advanced Fab, using solder_paste, lens_assembly, gold_wire, and steel_rod, with cycle times ranging from 16.0 weeks to 22.0 weeks. Packaging support is available through the Packaging Machine, which has capacity 1, works at an average service time of 1.851 weeks, batches 29 units at a time, waits up to 7.176 weeks to form a batch, and costs $0.197 per week to run. On the demand side, Bosch Automotive buys smartphone units, placing orders every 23.0 weeks with demand ranging from 2376734.0 units to 2687715.0 units per order. Customer delivery takes between 2.0 weeks and 17.0 weeks, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered, the selling price is $4312.427 per unit, and payment comes 46.0 days later. NXP Semiconductors purchases EV_battery units every 37.0 weeks in fixed lots of 4625878.0 units, with a customer lead time of exactly 29.0 weeks. Here the business follows a partial-fill lost-sales approach: available units are shipped, and any remaining demand is lost. The selling price is $4644.941 per unit, and customer payment arrives between 17.0 days and 66.0 days after shipment. Structurally, MegaSupply, NanoMaterials Inc., GlobalComponents, FastChip Corp., and ChipCo all feed Advanced Fab, and Advanced Fab then sends both smartphone units and EV_battery units to the Distribution Center. The model runs in weeks over a 200-week horizon with 10 replications.

