rtages cost $25.337 per unit, likewise reviewed every 1 hour. Supplier coverage is diversified. ChipCo provides gold_wire with a fixed 26.0-hour lead time at $261.348 per unit, and payment is due between 23.0 hours and 46.0 hours after receipt. CarbonSupply Co. is another gold_wire source, with an exponential lead time averaging 9.0 hours, a price of $326.4 per unit, and net 39.0 hours payment. MetalFab Inc. also supplies gold_wire, typically arriving in 15.0 to 21.0 hours, at $291.371 per unit and payable after 78.0 hours. For carbon_fiber, Process Go. delivers in exactly 9.0 hours at $209.491 per unit, with 46.0-hour payment terms, and shipments to the Processing Unit take between 5.0 hours and 9.0 hours to transfer. ElectroParts offers a second carbon_fiber lane with a consistent 26.0-hour supplier lead time, a lower cost of $101.606 per unit, payment between 49.0 hours and 78.0 hours, and a supplier limit of 663276 units per delivery; its transfer to the plant takes 2.0 hours. PrecisionParts handles ceramic_substrate with a fixed 20.0-hour lead time, a very low $3.034 per unit cost, 87.0-hour payment terms, and a maximum order size of 338443 units. Aluminum_sheet comes from FastChip Corp., whose lead time is exponential with a mean of 9.0 hours, priced at $334.342 per unit, with payment due between 37.0 hours and 48.0 hours, and the transfer into the plant takes 9.0 hours flat. Production itself runs through the Processing Unit in several flows. Drone manufacturing uses a cutting step that consumes aluminum_sheet, battery_pack, and carbon_fiber, produces drone, and takes exactly 26.0 hours per cycle. That step requires the CNC Machine, which has capacity for 1 unit of work at a time, an exponential service time averaging 6.983 hours, batching enabled at 87 units, a maximum wait of 12.009 hours, and an operating cost of $8.635 per hour. Industrial_sensor production is another cutting process, this time using motor_assembly and frame_structure, and the cycle varie