 at 803830 units per order. NanoMaterials Inc. sends memory_chip in a consistent 23.0 hours at $207.807 per unit, with invoices settling somewhere between 29.0 and 75.0 days. Process Go. supplies memory_chip in a 7.0 to 25.0 hour window, at $32.381 per unit, with payment due between 23.0 and 33.0 days, and the transfer from that supplier to the Manufacturing Site takes 12.0 hours. Production is split across two activities at the Manufacturing Site. The drone line runs a polishing step that takes exactly 15.0 hours per cycle, uses memory_chip and circuit_board as inputs, produces drone, and requires the Robot Arm. That Robot Arm has capacity for 1 unit at a time, works with a service time ranging from 1.96 to 4.757 hours, and costs $18.707 per hour to operate. The solar_panel line uses a bonding step, converting copper_wire into solar_panel in a fixed 11.0 hour cycle. The site also has access to a Conveyor Belt with capacity of 5 units, service time between 3.13 and 8.114 hours, and an operating cost of $16.152 per hour. Finished drone and solar_panel output then move from the Manufacturing Site to the Fulfillment Hub. On the demand side, NXP Semiconductors buys drone, placing orders every 13.0 to 24.0 hours with a constant demand of 4734870.0 units per order. Delivery to that customer takes between 4.0 and 7.0 hours, the selling price is $3880.103 per unit, and payment arrives 76.0 days later. If stock is short, available units are shipped and the rest of the demand is lost. Infineon Technologies purchases solar_panel every 19.0 hours, with order sizes varying from 1751345.0 to 4681789.0 units, a customer lead time of exactly 26.0 hours, a price of $2069.3 per unit, and payment between 31.0 and 85.0 days; any unmet volume is backordered. Ross Associates also buys solar_panel, ordering every 38.0 hours with a fixed demand of 4108386.0 units, requiring shipment in 8.0 hours, paying $3036.198 per unit, and settling invoices after 87.0 days. In that case, available units go out immediately and the remainder is backordered. The model runs in hours over a 730 hour horizon, with results collected after a 50 hour warm-up period.

