This setup revolves around producing a medical_device through Main Factory, with Logistics Center handling downstream storage and flow, while GlassCore Ltd. and MetalFab Inc. feed the plant with solder_paste and aluminum_sheet. The product structure is layered: each cooling_unit is built from 1 unit of solder_paste and 4 units of aluminum_sheet, and each medical_device then uses 1 unit of aluminum_sheet, 1 unit of cooling_unit, and 3 units of solder_paste. At the raw material level, solder_paste is supplied on a very infrequent fixed cycle of 87949.0 hours, with deliveries arriving somewhere between 9.0 hours and 14.0 hours, and it carries a holding cost of $7.856 per unit with inventory reviewed every 3 hours. That material comes from GlassCore Ltd., which delivers in exactly 5.0 hours, charges $346.248 per unit, and offers payment terms ranging from 9.0 days to 44.0 days after receipt. Aluminum_sheet, by contrast, is sourced as needed based on demand, held at a cost of $7.852 per unit, and reviewed every 23 hours. MetalFab Inc. supplies it with a fixed 28.0-hour lead time, at $289.409 per unit, with payment due 52.0 days after delivery. Inside the operation, Main Factory manages aluminum_sheet, solder_paste, cooling_unit, and medical_device inventory, starting with 452824 units of cooling_unit on hand and 3900706 units of medical_device in stock. The molding step at Main Factory consumes aluminum_sheet, cooling_unit, and solder_paste to produce medical_device, and each run takes between 16.0 hours and 19.0 hours. This activity requires the Quality Scanner, which has capacity for 4 units, processes work in anywhere from 0.361 hours to 9.809 hours, and runs in batches of 48 units with a maximum wait of 13.929 hours before release. The scanner is not perfectly reliable either: it stays up for a consistent 430.45 hours, then goes down for 8.937 hours, and it costs $7.399 per hour to operate. On the market side, TechCorp buys the medical_device, with order arrivals averaging every 25.0 hours, demand centered around 2190281.0 units with variability of 463874.0 units, and a customer lead time fixed at 25.0 hours. If demand exceeds what is available, the business ships what it can and loses the remainder. The selling price is $2643.234 per unit, and customer payment comes 87.0 days later. Network-wise, both GlassCore Ltd. and MetalFab Inc. connect into Main Factory, and finished medical_device units move from Main Factory to Logistics Center. The model runs for 200 hours in total, with results collected after a 50-hour warm-up period, across 5 replications.

